  "verbalization": "Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool appears to interact with Tankyrase-2 through a series of molecular pathways, with the primary interaction occurring via the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme. This enzyme is a target of Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool and is itself a target of multiple other molecules, including Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate. These latter molecules are not directly linked to Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool, but their shared targeting of Tankyrase-2 suggests a potential downstream effect. The evidence suggests that Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool may influence Tankyrase-2 through a chain of enzymatic interactions, where the compound acts as a modulator of the downstream pathways that ultimately affect Tankyrase-2. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility of a regulatory mechanism involving the sialyltransferase enzyme, which could be a key mediator in the relationship between Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool and Tankyrase-2.",
